            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a commotion, then the Arabic for a crowd."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: مظاهرة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مظاهرة — muẓāhara — \"a demonstration, a march\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سار الطلاب في مظاهرة سلمية. sāra aṭ-ṭullāb fī muẓāhara silmiyya. The students walked in a peaceful march."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مظاهرة (muẓāhara) is built on the native Arabic root ẓ-h-r (Lane), the root of ẓahr, the back, and ẓahara, to appear. Form III ẓāhara is \"to back someone up\"; a public show of support is the modern sense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
