              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هتف — hatafa — \"to cheer, to chant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هتف الأطفال فرحا. hatafa al-aṭfāl faraḥan. The children cheered for joy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يهتف, yahtif."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The taught هاتف, a telephone, is the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هتف (hatafa) is usually traced to the native Arabic root h-t-f, \"to call out\", where hātif was a voice heard when the speaker is not seen; modern Arabic gave that word the telephone."
            }
          ]
        },
